    "ask.h.t.justNow":         { zh: "刚刚",               en: "Just now" },
    "ask.h.t.5min":            { zh: "5 分钟前",           en: "5 min ago" },
    "ask.h.t.today09":         { zh: "今日 09:01",         en: "Today 09:01" },
    "ask.h.t.yesterday":       { zh: "昨日",               en: "Yesterday" },
    "ask.h.t.may7":            { zh: "5月7日",             en: "May 7" },
    "ask.h.t.may5":            { zh: "5月5日",             en: "May 5" },
    "ask.h.t.may3":            { zh: "5月3日",             en: "May 3" },
    "ask.answer.lede.html":    { zh: "您的两篇收藏（<em>RMT v3</em>、<em>MemGPT</em>）代表两种处理\"超出训练长度上下文\"的根本不同范式 —— 这一区别在生产系统中带来 <strong>数量级的成本差异</strong>，因此值得您关心。",
                                  en: "Your two saves (<em>RMT v3</em>, <em>MemGPT</em>) represent two fundamentally different paradigms for handling «context that exceeds training length» — a distinction that produces <strong>order-of-magnitude cost differences</strong> in production. Worth your attention." },
    "ask.answer.h1":           { zh: "核心区别 · 一句话版",  en: "Core difference · one-line version" },
    "ask.answer.p1.html":      { zh: "<strong>RMT v3</strong> 通过<em>循环压缩</em>把整段上下文塞进固定长度的隐状态，让模型在 2M token 上保持 O(n) 复杂度<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"1\">1</a>；<strong>MemGPT</strong> 则把模型本身当作\"操作系统\"，通过 <em>显式记忆调度</em>（main context ↔ recall storage）来按需调入信息<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"2\">2</a>。前者是\"编译进权重的隐式压缩\"；后者是\"运行时显式的换页机制\"。",
                                  en: "<strong>RMT v3</strong> uses <em>recurrent compression</em> to stuff entire context into a fixed-length hidden state, holding O(n) at 2M tokens<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"1\">1</a>; <strong>MemGPT</strong> treats the model itself as an «operating system», using <em>explicit memory scheduling</em> (main context ↔ recall storage) to swap in information as needed<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"2\">2</a>. The former is «implicit compression baked into weights»; the latter is «explicit run-time paging»." },
    "ask.answer.h2":           { zh: "三个您应该关心的实际差异",  en: "Three practical differences worth your attention" },
    "ask.answer.li1.html":     { zh: "<strong>训练 vs 推理时机会成本：</strong>RMT v3 需要重新训练或继续训练 base model<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"1\">1</a>；MemGPT 可在<em>冻结权重</em>下使用，与您 4月17日收藏的 LongMem 同属此阵营<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"3\">3</a>。",
                                  en: "<strong>Training vs inference-time opportunity cost:</strong> RMT v3 requires retraining or continued training of the base model<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"1\">1</a>; MemGPT runs on <em>frozen weights</em>, in the same camp as the LongMem paper you saved on Apr 17<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"3\">3</a>." },
    "ask.answer.li2.html":     { zh: "<strong>显存占用：</strong>RMT v3 的隐状态显存恒定；MemGPT 的 main context 仍受标准 KV cache 限制 —— 在 200K 模式下 KV cache 占用可达 <strong>~125GB / 70B 模型</strong>（您 4月22日的笔记 #2204 中已有计算）。",
                                  en: "<strong>VRAM footprint:</strong> RMT v3's hidden-state memory is constant; MemGPT's main context is still bounded by standard KV cache — at 200K, KV cache reaches <strong>~125 GB on a 70B model</strong> (your note #2204 from Apr 22 has the math)." },
    "ask.answer.li3.html":     { zh: "<strong>失败模式：</strong>RMT v3 在叙事文本上压缩损失 ≤ 2.3%，但代码与表格任务上被 Anthropic 测得 14.7%<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"1\">1</a>；MemGPT 的失败模式是<em>调度策略</em>不当时的\"换页抖动\"，需要工程化调优。",
                                  en: "<strong>Failure modes:</strong> RMT v3 keeps compression loss ≤ 2.3% on narrative text, but Anthropic measured 14.7% on code and tabular tasks<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"1\">1</a>; MemGPT's failure mode is «paging thrash» under bad scheduling — it needs engineering tuning." },
    "ask.answer.h3":           { zh: "Lilian Weng 的反方意见",  en: "Lilian Weng's opposing take" },
    "ask.answer.p2.html":      { zh: "值得注意的是 5月3日 Lilian Weng 在博客中指出：即便上下文塞得下，注意力稀释也会造成多跳任务准确率下降 —— 因此\"长窗口的承诺在生产中被高估了\"<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"4\">4</a>。这间接支持 MemGPT 路线在工程上的合理性。",
                                  en: "Worth noting: on May 3, Lilian Weng argued on her blog that even when the context fits, attention dilution still erodes multi-hop accuracy — hence «the promise of long windows is overstated in production»<a class=\"cite\" data-src=\"4\">4</a>. This indirectly supports MemGPT's engineering case." },
    "ask.answer.curatorTake":  { zh: "CURATOR&rsquo;S TAKE",  en: "CURATOR&rsquo;S TAKE" },
    "ask.answer.curator.html": { zh: "如果您正在做 <em>会话型 agent</em>（多轮、长 horizon），MemGPT 范式的可控性更高；如果您在做 <em>批处理文档分析</em>（一次性长输入），RMT v3 的成本曲线更优。两者在 2026 H2 大概率会被某种<strong>双层混合架构</strong>统一。",
                                  en: "If you're building a <em>conversational agent</em> (multi-turn, long horizon), MemGPT gives you more control; if you're doing <em>batch document analysis</em> (one-shot long inputs), RMT v3's cost curve wins. Both will likely be unified under some <strong>two-tier hybrid architecture</strong> by 2026 H2." },
